1
00:00:00,950 --> 00:00:02,190
Good evening, excellence…

2
00:00:02,360 --> 00:00:04,390
Bring the last SWOT analysis you did…

3
00:00:04,490 --> 00:00:05,350
and tell me:

4
00:00:05,740 --> 00:00:07,100
how many decisions came out of it?

5
00:00:07,220 --> 00:00:09,590
Usually… four boxes full of words,

6
00:00:09,870 --> 00:00:11,110
then put away in a drawer.

7
00:00:11,330 --> 00:00:13,720
Before: SWOT = a list.

8
00:00:14,050 --> 00:00:16,500
After: SWOT = decisions.

9
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:18,470
Take a garment factory:

10
00:00:18,690 --> 00:00:21,090
its strength: tailoring quality,

11
00:00:21,450 --> 00:00:23,590
its weakness: marketing abroad,

12
00:00:23,960 --> 00:00:26,070
the opportunity: an export order,

13
00:00:26,100 --> 00:00:28,060
the threat: price competition.

14
00:00:28,180 --> 00:00:29,680
Link the boxes together:

15
00:00:29,870 --> 00:00:32,310
Strength + Opportunity: export on quality.

16
00:00:32,670 --> 00:00:34,150
Weakness + Opportunity: partner

17
00:00:34,150 --> 00:00:35,630
with an export agency.

18
00:00:35,860 --> 00:00:37,335
Strength + Threat: compete

19
00:00:37,335 --> 00:00:38,810
on quality, not price.

20
00:00:39,080 --> 00:00:40,565
Weakness + Threat: start

21
00:00:40,565 --> 00:00:42,050
with a small order.

22
00:00:42,170 --> 00:00:44,830
This is called the TOWS matrix.

23
00:00:45,070 --> 00:00:46,220
Remember it this way:

24
00:00:46,220 --> 00:00:47,840
An analysis that produces no decision…

25
00:00:47,950 --> 00:00:48,960
is useless.

26
00:00:49,180 --> 00:00:50,920
And you? Your last SWOT…

27
00:00:50,920 --> 00:00:52,180
how many decisions did it produce?

28
00:00:52,540 --> 00:00:54,090
Tell me in the comments.

29
00:00:54,400 --> 00:00:56,100
See you next episode…

30
00:00:56,170 --> 00:00:57,700
on Masaa Al-Tamayoz
